---
export const prerender = true;
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
import { TRUST_CONFIG } from "../lib/trust-config";

const effectiveDate = new Date(TRUST_CONFIG.policyEffectiveDate).toLocaleDateString("en-GB", {
  day: "numeric",
  month: "long",
  year: "numeric",
  timeZone: "UTC",
});
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Terms of Service | CrawlPact"
  description="Terms governing use of CrawlPact's website, free audit tool, and subscription plans."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-reading px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-h1 text-neutral-950">Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-supporting text-neutral-500">
      Effective and last updated: {effectiveDate}.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">1. Agreement</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">Using CrawlPact means you agree to these terms.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">2. Operator</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      {TRUST_CONFIG.legalEntityName} operates the CrawlPact service.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">3. Eligibility and authority</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      You must be able to enter into this agreement, and must have authority to use any account
      information you submit. CrawlPact does not verify legal ownership of a domain you submit for
      audit — see "Acceptable use" below for the actual scope of permitted use.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">4. Account responsibilities</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">You are responsible for:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 text-body text-neutral-700">
      <li>Providing accurate account information</li>
      <li>The security of your passkey credentials and any recovery codes</li>
      <li>Activity that occurs under your account</li>
      <li>Notifying CrawlPact promptly if you suspect your account has been compromised</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">5. The service</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact audits and monitors the publicly declared AI crawler policy of a website you
      specify: saved domains, scheduled monitoring, findings, evidence-based recommendations,
      crawler-registry versions, and reporting, with paid-plan limits as described on{" "}
      <a href="/pricing" class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">pricing</a>. CrawlPact
      evaluates and reports on declared policy and observed public responses; it does not prove or
      guarantee that any crawler will obey that policy.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">6. Product boundaries</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 text-body text-neutral-700">
      <li>CrawlPact audits public policy signals.</li>
      <li>CrawlPact does not control external crawlers.</li>
      <li>
        CrawlPact does not guarantee crawler compliance, search inclusion, or training exclusion.
      </li>
      <li>CrawlPact is not legal advice and is not a legal compliance certification.</li>
      <li>CrawlPact does not replace a WAF, CDN, or bot-management service.</li>
      <li>Results may change when a website's declared policy or the crawler registry changes.</li>
      <li>Public resources CrawlPact depends on may be unavailable or incomplete at scan time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">7. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">You must not use CrawlPact to:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 text-body text-neutral-700">
      <li>Break the law, or use the service for an unlawful purpose</li>
      <li>Interfere with or disrupt CrawlPact's infrastructure</li>
      <li>Attempt to bypass rate limits or automate high-volume use without approval</li>
      <li>
        Attempt security testing of CrawlPact's own systems without authorisation — see <a
          href="/security"
          class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">security</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>Submit a target for the purpose of probing or attacking internal infrastructure</li>
      <li>Misrepresent an audit result as a guarantee of crawler compliance</li>
      <li>Resell or white-label CrawlPact contrary to your plan's terms</li>
      <li>Engage in fraudulent billing behaviour</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">8. User-submitted domains and public resources</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      The free audit is designed to let you analyse any public domain, and CrawlPact does not verify
      domain ownership before running one. You are responsible for using CrawlPact lawfully and
      responsibly, and must not use it to harass, probe, or attack a website you do not operate.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">9. Crawler registry and methodology</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 text-body text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        Registry information is evidence-based but can change as operator documentation changes.
      </li>
      <li>
        Crawler-purpose classifications may contain uncertainty, and are labelled honestly rather
        than guessed.
      </li>
      <li>Reports identify the registry version they were evaluated against, where supported.</li>
      <li>
        Corrections may be submitted to <a
          href={`mailto:${TRUST_CONFIG.correctionsContact}`}
          class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">{TRUST_CONFIG.correctionsContact}</a
        > — see <a
          href="/methodology#corrections"
          class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">how corrections are reviewed</a
        >.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">10. Recommendations and decisions</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      You remain responsible for your own policy objectives, website configuration, legal decisions,
      business decisions, implementation, and monitoring responses. CrawlPact's recommendations are
      not guaranteed outcomes.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">11. Paid plans and billing</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      Paid plans are billed annually through {TRUST_CONFIG.billingProvider}, acting as merchant of
      record. {TRUST_CONFIG.merchantOfRecordDescription} Paddle handles payment collection, tax calculation,
      receipts, renewal, and cancellation. CrawlPact does not store your payment-card details, though
      it does retain billing metadata (a Paddle customer/subscription identifier, transaction status,
      and amounts) necessary for entitlements, support, and accounting.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      Subscriptions are cancelled through Paddle's customer portal, linked from your account's
      billing settings. When a subscription's Paddle status changes to cancelled, expired, or
      paused, your account moves to the Free plan. Plan limits and upgrade/downgrade behaviour are
      described on <a href="/pricing" class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">pricing</a
      >. A failed payment does not immediately end access — Paddle retries payment during a grace
      period, during which your plan remains active.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">12. Refunds</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact does not independently issue refunds; refund and chargeback decisions are handled by {
        TRUST_CONFIG.billingProvider
      } as merchant of record. For a refund enquiry, contact{" "}
      <a
        href={`mailto:${TRUST_CONFIG.billingContact}`}
        class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">{TRUST_CONFIG.billingContact}</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">13. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact's software, brand, documentation, methodology, and crawler-registry compilation are
      owned by {TRUST_CONFIG.legalEntityName}. CrawlPact does not claim ownership over third-party
      crawler-operator documentation or the content of websites you audit.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">14. Feedback</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      If you send CrawlPact feedback or suggestions, CrawlPact may use them to improve the service
      without owing you compensation, but this does not affect any separate rights you have in your
      own account data or audited website content.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">15. Third-party services</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact relies on {TRUST_CONFIG.infrastructureProviders.join(", ")} for infrastructure and{
        " "
      }
      {TRUST_CONFIG.billingProvider} for billing. Their own terms apply to their respective services.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">16. Availability and changes</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      The service may change — features may be added, modified, or discontinued, and maintenance or
      incidents may occur. Current operational status is available on the{" "}
      <a href="/status" class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">status page</a>.
      CrawlPact does not promise uninterrupted availability.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">17. Suspension and termination</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact may suspend or terminate access on reasonable grounds, including abuse, non-payment,
      a security risk, a legal requirement, or a violation of these terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">18. Disclaimers</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis, to the extent permitted by
      applicable law. Nothing in these terms excludes a right that cannot lawfully be excluded.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">19. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, CrawlPact's liability arising from your use
      of the service is limited to the amount you paid CrawlPact in the twelve months before the
      claim arose. This section does not limit liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">20. No guarantee of outcome</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact does not guarantee that any AI crawler will honour a declared policy, that content
      will or will not appear in an AI system's output, or any specific search or AI visibility
      outcome.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">21. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      These terms may be updated as the product develops. Material changes are reflected on this
      page with a new "effective and last updated" date above.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">22. Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      For general terms and support matters, contact{" "}
      <a
        href={`mailto:${TRUST_CONFIG.supportContact}`}
        class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">{TRUST_CONFIG.supportContact}</a
      >. For privacy-related issues, contact{" "}
      <a
        href={`mailto:${TRUST_CONFIG.privacyContact}`}
        class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">{TRUST_CONFIG.privacyContact}</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>
